## Notes against the acceptance criteria

| AC | How it's met |
|---|---|
| 1. Bucket | `BucketVersioningV2` Enabled, `AES256` SSE + bucket keys, `BucketPublicAccessBlock` all-true, TLS-only bucket policy. Prod adds CRR to `us-west-2` with its own versioned/encrypted/private replica. |
| 2. RDS | `deletionProtection: true` in both envs, `publiclyAccessible: false`, `backupRetentionPeriod` from config with a build-time guard rejecting `< 7`, final snapshot required. Prod also `multiAz` + `protect: true`. |
| 3. Secret | Password generated by `random.RandomPassword` — never in Git. Connection string wrapped in `pulumi.secret()` so it is encrypted by the stack's secrets provider in state, and mirrored to Secrets Manager for runtime consumption. |
| 4. IAM | IRSA trust scoped to one `system:serviceaccount:<ns>:<name>` and `sts.amazonaws.com` audience. Policy lists explicit actions; resources are the exact bucket ARN, `arn/*`, and the one secret ARN. No `*` actions in any env. |
| 7. Isolation | Each stack has its own state and its own config file; `pulumi up -s prod` touches only prod resources. The component takes VPC/subnet/OIDC inputs, so nothing is shared implicitly. |

Cluster (EKS) and HTTPS/CloudFront live in sibling components (`ClusterStack`, `EdgeStack`) composed the same way in `index.ts`; this component covers the bucket/RDS/IAM slice requested.

**Deploy:**

```bash
pulumi stack init dev  && pulumi up -s dev
pulumi stack init prod && pulumi up -s prod
```

For a shared KMS-backed secrets provider instead of the default passphrase:

```bash
pulumi stack init prod --secrets-provider="awskms://alias/pulumi-prod?region=us-east-1"
```
